Candida albicans Agent-Based Model (ABM)

This repository contains an Agent-Based Model built in Julia to simulate the population dynamics and evolutionary survival strategies of single-celled organisms (Candida albicans). Specifically, it investigates whether Programmed Cell Death (PCD) provides a colony-level survival advantage under antifungal stress.

📂 Repository Structure

To ensure the scripts run correctly, maintain the following folder structure:

Project_Root/
│
├── Code/
│   ├── core_model.jl                  # The main ABM mechanics, agent definitions, and step logic
│   ├── experiment_uniform_nutrient.jl # The experiment script running the sweep
│   └── ... (other experiment scripts)
│
├── Data/                              # CSV outputs will be automatically saved here
│
└── Figures/                           # Plot images will be automatically saved here


⚙️ Prerequisites & Setup

Install Julia: Download and install Julia from julialang.org.

Install Required Packages: Open your terminal or command prompt, type julia to open the REPL, and run the following commands to install the necessary libraries:

using Pkg
Pkg.add("Agents")
Pkg.add("DataFrames")
Pkg.add("CSV")
Pkg.add("Plots")
Pkg.add("StatsBase")
Pkg.add("Images")
Pkg.add("ImageFiltering")


🚀 How to Run the Experiments

Because the scripts use universal relative pathing (@__DIR__), you can run them from anywhere on your computer.

Option 1: Using the Terminal / Command Prompt

Open your terminal.

Navigate to the folder containing the scripts (or run them directly).

Execute the script:

julia Code/experiment_uniform_nutrient.jl


Option 2: Using an IDE (VS Code, Jupyter, etc.)
Simply open the experiment script (e.g., experiment_uniform_nutrient.jl) in your preferred editor and run the file.

📊 Outputs

When you run an experiment script:

It automatically includes the core_model.jl engine.

It executes a sweep across defined parameters (e.g., Antifungal Doses vs. Apoptosis Binding Capacity).

A .csv file containing the step-by-step population data is saved to the Data/ folder.

A grid plot (.png) visually comparing the survival curves is saved to the Figures/ folder.
